  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency health assistance to displaced conflict-affected refugees and returnees in Unity and Upper Nile States in South Sudan.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide health assistance to vulnerable people in South Sudan fleeing fighting in Sudan. This WHO project will provide emergency health kits to health facilities, provide primary health care consultations, and support disease outbreak surveillance. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 100,000 people, including 40,809 women, 23,002 children, and 14,998 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
